{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation deviation (recorded, not silent): the plan places the re-score script at reports/llm-gate-cost-2026-08-11/round2/plan_v5_rescore.py, but /reports/ is GITIGNORED (.gitignore:95), so a script there could never land and the AC's proving command would be unrunnable in any other checkout. Landed instead at docs/calibration/plan_v5_rescore.py, beside its write-up docs/calibration/plan_v5_kind_sets.md — which is also what the operator's original instruction said (re-score output under docs/calibration/). It takes --root=<checkout> because the corpus lives in .tickets-tracker/ and a fresh worktree has none. Second, a real bug the gate caught in my own evidence script: computing the OLD baseline by calling the shipped impact_plan is invalid once the conversion lands, because the new function scores the corpus's ordinal grades as 0.0 — the baseline collapses (2897 -> 2691) and the comparison reports lost=0 regardless of the change's effect. The script now pins legacy_impact_plan() reproducing the plan-v4 formula explicitly. Final result over 22,665 findings: old 2,897 at/above bar; pessimistic residual lost 47 gained 35; optimistic lost 15 gained 64; all 15 hard losses audited, every one a bundling or specificity/framing finding. Zero unjustified losses - R1 says land."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786515097507997001,"uuid":"1bda1a9e-1878-4b77-abef-693549137d1c"}